From: Nerves Gate <nerves-gate@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: treat the shared USB PHY IRQ as optional

RK3506 uses the per-port interrupts. The driver already supports an absent
shared IRQ, but platform_get_irq emits an error before that fallback. Use
the optional accessor and preserve deferred probing.

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -2536,7 +2536,9 @@
 	rphy->chg_state = USB_CHG_STATE_UNDEFINED;
 	rphy->chg_type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_UNKNOWN;
 	rphy->edev_self = false;
-	rphy->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
+	rphy->irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);
+	if (rphy->irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, rphy);
 
 	ret = rockchip_usb2phy_extcon_register(rphy);
